@startuml architecture-overview
title Runtime Architecture: HTTP Control Plane and TCP P2P Data Plane

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "Browser A" as BrowserA
actor "Browser B" as BrowserB

package "Control Plane - HTTP" {
  component "sampleapp A\nHTTP API\n:2026" as SampleA
  component "sampleapp B\nHTTP API\n:2027" as SampleB
  component "trackerapp\nPeer registry\nChannel metadata\n:9000" as Tracker
  database "db/users.json\nactive_sessions.json" as AuthStore
}

package "Data Plane - TCP P2P" {
  component "PeerManager A\nTCP listener\n:9101" as PeerA
  component "PeerManager B\nTCP listener\n:9102" as PeerB
}

package "DHT Overlay (Channeling)" {
  component "DHTOverlay A\nsuccessor/finger state" as DhtA
  component "DHTOverlay B\nsuccessor/finger state" as DhtB
}

BrowserA --> SampleA : HTTP UI/API\nlogin, peers, connect, send
BrowserB --> SampleB : HTTP UI/API\nlogin, peers, connect, send

SampleA --> AuthStore : validate credentials\ncreate session cookie
SampleB --> AuthStore : validate credentials\ncreate session cookie

SampleA --> Tracker : /register\n/heartbeat\n/peers\n/channels
SampleB --> Tracker : /register\n/heartbeat\n/peers\n/channels

SampleA --> PeerA : local method calls\nconnect_peer, send_chat
SampleB --> PeerB : local method calls\nconnect_peer, send_chat

PeerA <--> PeerB : TCP P2P frames\n4-byte length + JSON\nhello/chat/ack/ping/pong/goodbye

DhtA --> PeerA : uses PeerManager transport
DhtB --> PeerB : uses PeerManager transport
DhtA <..> DhtB : DHT routing for channels\nowner lookup (successor)\nowner fan-out saves resources

@enduml
